Chapter: ProbeClosureReturn

 Minimal: does a definition whose RETURN TYPE is a function compile, and
 what does bare metal do with it? Found while writing tier 13, where
 `make-adder : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)` dumped registers
 on bare metal instead of answering or refusing.

 Expected if the shape is legal: `applied 47` then `recursed 47`.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

  make-adder : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  make-adder (n) = add3 n

 The same definition, but reaching its result through a SELF TAIL CALL.
 Bare metal turns a self tail call into a jump; the value being returned
 here is a closure rather than a word.

  count-down : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  count-down (n) = if n == 0 then add3 5 else count-down (n - 1)

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("applied " & show (((make-adder 5) 20) 22))
    print-line-uni ("recursed " & show (((count-down 3) 20) 22))
  end
